   "sign_meaning_bank_all_rows": "The as-published index is the smallest eigenvalue of the S_b-scaled Schur complement S_GG - S_GF S_FF^-1 S_FG of the loads-out stiffened matrix S (Y_eq of eq. 33 in symmetric form), so a nonpositive value means that this Schur complement is not positive definite. S_FF is positive definite on all 7324 rows, so by Haynsworth's inertia additivity the index is nonpositive exactly where S itself, over all 10 plants, has a nonpositive eigenvalue (366 rows of the bank). On those rows eq. 39's second form, 1/lambda_max(Z S_b), is not the index: it is positive on 366 of them."
